      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "i don't understand how exactly this works, it seems like once a day i have to log back in even if i was logged just an hour earlier.  and each time this happens, i have to shut down vrchat, walk back to my computer, reboot steamvr, log into desktop mode and type in my password because doing it in vr is maddening.  since you'd have to have placed the headset at just the right angle to easily reach the virtual keys, but even there it's too easy to make a mistake and have to retype my entire email and long password again.  so, instead we have to exit everything and try again, and because there's other bugs, sometimes during this process other things happen, such as losing audio so then i have to try a third time after going into steamvr and resetting the audio card.  this is one of a few things that makes logging in a big pain in the butt!  and used to not be needed, but for some reason now it times out, pleaaaase fix this.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
